WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.600
<v DANA>A needle can push through the fingertip of a thick work glove.

2
00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:10.080
<v DANA>So say a plant has to choose. Thicker gloves for everyone who handles the trash, or

3
00:00:10.240 --> 00:00:13.760
<v DANA>more sharps containers, like the kind mounted on a break-room wall.

4
00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:16.920
<v DANA>I'd have bought the gloves. Which would you pick?

5
00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:22.880
<v RAY>The containers. Gloves are P-P-E, the protective gear you wear, and P-P-E alone

6
00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:26.640
<v RAY>works less well against needlesticks than engineering controls.

7
00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:30.400
<v RAY>An engineering control is something built into the workplace, like that container on

8
00:00:30.440 --> 00:00:34.880
<v RAY>the wall. The best protection is a proper sharps container, because it takes the

9
00:00:34.987 --> 00:00:37.232
<v RAY>hazard away before anyone can touch it.

10
00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:40.080
<v DANA>Then those gloves would just be for show?

11
00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:45.440
<v RAY>No, they earn their place. Heavy-duty gloves made of nitrile, latex, vinyl or

12
00:00:45.520 --> 00:00:49.840
<v RAY>neoprene can protect your hands from cuts and from hazardous substances.

13
00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:52.160
<v RAY>I just wouldn't count on them against a needle.

14
00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:56.000
<v DANA>Walk me through what the container actually changes out on a plant floor.

15
00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:01.400
<v RAY>A safety-engineered sharps container closes the sharp inside the moment it drops in.

16
00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:05.520
<v RAY>In manufacturing settings, that cuts down on accidental needlesticks, and on

17
00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:08.640
<v RAY>bloodborne pathogens passing from one person to another.

18
00:01:08.640 --> 00:01:12.640
<v DANA>So once the containers are up, do they do the job by themselves?

19
00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:18.080
<v RAY>No. People lean toward the easiest path, and the containers and the training both

20
00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:23.120
<v RAY>have to beat that habit. At more than one plant, I've watched people walk RIGHT past

21
00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:25.120
<v RAY>a container to the nearest trash bin.
